WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.301 --> 00:00:04.468
- I've been through the
toughest times with my family,

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:07.310
but I'm still standing.

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:09.728
It was kind of tough
knowin' that sometimes

00:00:09.728 --> 00:00:11.228
I would work so hard than everybody else,

00:00:11.228 --> 00:00:13.705
and I wasn't seein', I wasn't
reapin' the benefits of it,

00:00:13.705 --> 00:00:14.538
and I wasn't...

00:00:14.538 --> 00:00:17.703
I means people just always say that,

00:00:17.703 --> 00:00:19.663
"It's cool, you're top
three, that's cool."

00:00:19.663 --> 00:00:23.246
And a lot of people got on
me for cryin' on national TV,

00:00:23.246 --> 00:00:26.091
but when you want somethin'
that bad, it's just like,

00:00:26.091 --> 00:00:26.924
I didn't care.

00:00:26.924 --> 00:00:28.289
You know, we talk about the end result,

00:00:28.289 --> 00:00:31.090
if it's not where it should
be, then it's a failure.

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:33.663
When something good happens
to you, I don't know

00:00:33.663 --> 00:00:35.883
about you guys, but I tend to look back

00:00:35.883 --> 00:00:37.495
to what brought me here.

00:00:37.495 --> 00:00:39.464
- He's an American
professional basketball player

00:00:39.464 --> 00:00:41.511
for the Oklahoma City Thunder of the NBA.

00:00:41.511 --> 00:00:44.361
- He's won an NBA
Most-Valuable Player award,

00:00:44.361 --> 00:00:48.103
four NBA scoring titles, and
the Rookie of the Year award.

00:00:48.103 --> 00:00:50.298
- He's been selected to six all-NBA teams

00:00:50.298 --> 00:00:52.110
and seven All-Star teams.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:55.057
- He's Kevin Durant and here's
my take on his top ten rules

00:00:55.057 --> 00:00:56.057
for success.

00:00:59.287 --> 00:01:01.120
- I come from a small,

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:05.018
county outside of Washington D.C.,

00:01:05.018 --> 00:01:07.202
called P.G. county.

00:01:07.202 --> 00:01:09.293
Me, my mom, my brother,

00:01:09.293 --> 00:01:12.274
we moved so many different
places growin' up,

00:01:12.274 --> 00:01:14.274
and, it felt like a box.

00:01:15.672 --> 00:01:19.279
It felt like there was no gettin' out.

00:01:19.279 --> 00:01:21.973
I loved basketball so
much, I loved playin' it,

00:01:21.973 --> 00:01:26.844
I just never thought I could
make it to college, NBA,

00:01:26.844 --> 00:01:28.471
or stand up here today
in front of you guys

00:01:28.471 --> 00:01:29.888
and be a NBA MVP.

00:01:31.098 --> 00:01:33.764
So many people believed in
me when I didn't believe

00:01:33.764 --> 00:01:34.597
in myself.

00:01:36.005 --> 00:01:38.897
So many people doubted me

00:01:38.897 --> 00:01:42.980
and motivated me every
single day to be who I am.

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:47.720
I failed so many times and got back up.

00:01:52.353 --> 00:01:56.520
I've been through the
toughest times with my family.

00:01:57.441 --> 00:01:59.441
But, I'm still standin'.

00:02:00.906 --> 00:02:04.609
- [Announcer] You continue
to put the ball in his hands.

00:02:04.609 --> 00:02:05.966
Durant comin' to the rim.

00:02:05.966 --> 00:02:08.049
I'll bring the...

00:02:08.049 --> 00:02:10.299
(laughing)

00:02:11.221 --> 00:02:12.971
Oh, big ol' tomahawk.

00:02:13.923 --> 00:02:16.405
- It was kind of tough
knowin' that sometimes

00:02:16.405 --> 00:02:18.041
I would work so hard than everyone else

00:02:18.041 --> 00:02:20.274
and I wasn't reapin' the benefits of it.

00:02:20.274 --> 00:02:23.695
I wasn't gettin' any better
as quickly as I wanted to,

00:02:23.695 --> 00:02:26.234
but I stayed patient, and
that was one big thing for me,

00:02:26.234 --> 00:02:27.835
is knowin' when to stay patient,

00:02:27.835 --> 00:02:29.337
that everything's going to come around.

00:02:29.337 --> 00:02:32.327
And I think that, you know,
with that patience I gained

00:02:32.327 --> 00:02:37.059
as a kid, it's helpin'
me in the NBA right now.

00:02:37.059 --> 00:02:39.948
For me, it's just, always,
always workin' hard

00:02:39.948 --> 00:02:41.523
and always tryin' to get better.

00:02:41.523 --> 00:02:42.976
And knowin' I can get better,

00:02:42.976 --> 00:02:45.670
knowin' that I'm not there where

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:49.587
I want to be yet, so, I
have a long ways to go.

00:02:52.084 --> 00:02:54.996
- [Announcer] Durant scoops
it up off the window,

00:02:54.996 --> 00:02:56.823
my goodness!

00:02:56.823 --> 00:03:00.258
Oh, the two-time scoring
champ showing you why.

00:03:00.258 --> 00:03:02.066
- Kevin, this is your quote,

00:03:02.066 --> 00:03:04.065
"I've been second my whole life,

00:03:04.065 --> 00:03:06.143
"I was the second best
player in high school,

00:03:06.143 --> 00:03:08.259
"second pick in the draft,

00:03:08.259 --> 00:03:10.664
"second in the MVP voting three times,

00:03:10.664 --> 00:03:14.560
"I came in second in the finals,
I'm tired of being second.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:19.088
"I'm not going to settle
for that, I'm done with it."

00:03:19.088 --> 00:03:20.564
Stand by that?

00:03:20.564 --> 00:03:21.647
- Definitely.

00:03:22.511 --> 00:03:26.076
I means people just always say that,

00:03:26.076 --> 00:03:28.218
"It's cool, you're top three, that's cool.

00:03:28.218 --> 00:03:32.165
"It's all right to be a top
three player in the world.

00:03:32.165 --> 00:03:33.423
"Millions of people in this world

00:03:33.423 --> 00:03:36.447
and you can be the top
three, that's pretty cool."

00:03:36.447 --> 00:03:39.682
I mean I'm just tired
of settlin' for that.

00:03:39.682 --> 00:03:43.242
Tired of sayin' that, tired of hearin' it.

00:03:43.242 --> 00:03:45.021
- [Announcer] Westbrook to
trigger at nine seconds,

00:03:45.021 --> 00:03:47.262
got to get it in, it's
in the hands of Durant,

00:03:47.262 --> 00:03:49.274
the scoring champ, from the top.

00:03:49.274 --> 00:03:52.169
Against Marion, Durant put up jumper,

00:03:52.169 --> 00:03:53.021
off the rim and it...

00:03:53.021 --> 00:03:54.033
(crowd cheering)

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.700
And the Thunder win!

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:59.153
Durant beat 'em again!

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:04.774
- [Announcer] All right let's go.

00:04:04.774 --> 00:04:06.562
- [Crowd Member] Let's go alright?

00:04:06.562 --> 00:04:09.513
- I work out on the court on
drills, but pick-up is where

00:04:09.513 --> 00:04:11.874
I hone my instincts for the game.

00:04:11.874 --> 00:04:14.564
- [Announcer] On his knees, up his throat.

00:04:14.564 --> 00:04:16.814
(cheering)

00:04:23.427 --> 00:04:25.862
- I love bein' around the atmosphere.

00:04:25.862 --> 00:04:27.725
I love bein' around basketball players,

00:04:27.725 --> 00:04:29.260
I love to hear the people talk trash

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:31.628
to me when I'm out in
the neighborhood playin'.

00:04:31.628 --> 00:04:35.795
I love it, that's the best
part of the summer to me.

00:04:38.167 --> 00:04:41.412
- [Announcer] The other
way, good rejection

00:04:41.412 --> 00:04:44.443
and block by Durant who comes galloping

00:04:44.443 --> 00:04:46.610
and Durant taking it down!

00:04:47.676 --> 00:04:51.806
Rockin' the rim, goin'
high and comin' down hard!

00:04:51.806 --> 00:04:54.827
(cheering)

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:56.371
- But, it's just a matter of me, you know,

00:04:56.371 --> 00:04:57.856
continuin' to learn the game and watch

00:04:57.856 --> 00:05:00.159
and try to get better each and every day.

00:05:00.159 --> 00:05:01.621
And, not being complacent,

00:05:01.621 --> 00:05:03.188
and I think that's the biggest thing,

00:05:03.188 --> 00:05:05.189
wanted to be great, but, in this game

00:05:05.189 --> 00:05:07.823
it's half and half mental and physical,

00:05:07.823 --> 00:05:10.498
maybe more mental than physical.

00:05:10.498 --> 00:05:12.853
So I got to get my mind
right and be able to handle

00:05:12.853 --> 00:05:17.020
a whole season and the
playoffs, to be a good player.

00:05:17.881 --> 00:05:20.742
But with me, it's just,
all about progressin'

00:05:20.742 --> 00:05:25.693
and knowin' what I need
to work on and work on it.

00:05:25.693 --> 00:05:28.940
- [Announcer] 23 points in their open...

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:31.106
What a move by Durant!

00:05:31.106 --> 00:05:34.889
And he let's the big doggy,
Collison, with the finish.

00:05:34.889 --> 00:05:37.711
- [Announcer] Adamovic
is still feeling that...

00:05:37.711 --> 00:05:39.235
- Oh, it was historical.

00:05:39.235 --> 00:05:40.777
I think about that run all the time.

00:05:40.777 --> 00:05:43.027
Oklahoma City is all about,

00:05:44.585 --> 00:05:46.983
first off natural disasters,

00:05:46.983 --> 00:05:49.366
and Oklahoma City bombin',
just to put it out there,

00:05:49.366 --> 00:05:51.782
to be real, I mean, that's
what the city was known for.

00:05:51.782 --> 00:05:54.995
And to win a Western
Conference title Championship

00:05:54.995 --> 00:05:56.570
with a group of young guys.

00:05:56.570 --> 00:05:58.904
The city's never seen anything like it

00:05:58.904 --> 00:06:00.889
and it's somethin'' I'm
always goin' to remember.

00:06:00.889 --> 00:06:02.916
- [Reporter] But the
Thunder lost the NBA title

00:06:02.916 --> 00:06:06.443
to the Miami Heat and
Lebron James in five games.

00:06:06.443 --> 00:06:08.787
Kevin Durant was second again,

00:06:08.787 --> 00:06:11.171
and there to console
him was the same person

00:06:11.171 --> 00:06:13.494
who made him do push-ups
in the middle of the night,

00:06:13.494 --> 00:06:15.227
12 years earlier.

00:06:15.227 --> 00:06:17.133
- [Interviewer] Long hug with your Mom,

00:06:17.133 --> 00:06:19.049
after you all didn't make it there,

00:06:19.049 --> 00:06:22.260
and you hugged her long and hard.

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:25.693
- (sighs) Well, first off,
that was just a thank you.

00:06:25.693 --> 00:06:29.457
My mom, she was always there
at the right time, man.

00:06:29.457 --> 00:06:33.095
And a lot of people got on
me for cryin' on national TV,

00:06:33.095 --> 00:06:35.529
but, when you want somethin' that bad,

00:06:35.529 --> 00:06:38.299
it was just like, I didn't care.

00:06:38.299 --> 00:06:40.899
- [Announcer] Be hard
pressed to beat 11.(laughs)

00:06:40.899 --> 00:06:44.158
I'm tellin' you that's hard
pressed to beat 11. (laughs)

00:06:44.158 --> 00:06:44.991
Durant to...

00:06:44.991 --> 00:06:46.427
Oh!

00:06:46.427 --> 00:06:47.260
K.D.

00:06:48.255 --> 00:06:49.704
packin' it.

00:06:49.704 --> 00:06:50.956
On McGee.

00:06:50.956 --> 00:06:52.206
The All-Top 10.

00:06:53.249 --> 00:06:55.507
- You know, in the first
few games of the playoffs

00:06:55.507 --> 00:06:59.178
I was just so excited to be a
part of that atmosphere again,

00:06:59.178 --> 00:07:02.021
and to be back on that
level, it was just amazin'.

00:07:02.021 --> 00:07:04.771
I appreciate every single moment,

00:07:07.192 --> 00:07:09.403
I always refer back to me bein' injured

00:07:09.403 --> 00:07:12.022
because that was the first
time something got taken away

00:07:12.022 --> 00:07:13.534
from me I loved so much,

00:07:13.534 --> 00:07:15.890
and it just made me appreciate
every moment, you know.

00:07:15.890 --> 00:07:20.440
Because we can easily talk
about the end result of things,

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:22.600
but that whole journey...

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:25.681
We talk about the end result
if it's not where it should be

00:07:25.681 --> 00:07:28.526
then it's a failure,
but I look at it like,

00:07:28.526 --> 00:07:30.974
look, this is an
important part of my life,

00:07:30.974 --> 00:07:33.341
this memory is somethin'
I'm always going to carry,

00:07:33.341 --> 00:07:36.305
and it was just great to be a part of,

00:07:36.305 --> 00:07:39.999
to be on the court playin'
in that atmosphere again.

00:07:39.999 --> 00:07:42.178
- [Announcer] Here we go,
tie game Wally has it,

00:07:42.178 --> 00:07:44.854
out front Durant, gets it
to a three for the win!

00:07:44.854 --> 00:07:46.399
It's already good!

00:07:46.399 --> 00:07:50.566
Kevin Durant, rises, reigns
and drains the 28 footer!

00:07:51.422 --> 00:07:54.239
The Sonics win in Atlanta,
you got to love it!

00:07:54.239 --> 00:07:56.748
- To always do it for the love,

00:07:56.748 --> 00:08:00.149
no matter what it is, and work
hard, it may sound cliche,

00:08:00.149 --> 00:08:04.923
but hard work really does
payoff in whatever you're doin'.

00:08:04.923 --> 00:08:07.697
That's the motto I use,
if you set small goals

00:08:07.697 --> 00:08:10.028
and try to reach them and
that's when big goals start

00:08:10.028 --> 00:08:12.729
to come around and, before you know it,

00:08:12.729 --> 00:08:16.396
you're goin' to start
risin' the totem pole.

00:08:18.904 --> 00:08:20.404
- Durant...
- Goal!

00:08:21.545 --> 00:08:24.188
Oh, my goodness, Roy Hibbert
couldn't get there in time

00:08:24.188 --> 00:08:25.021
on that.

00:08:25.021 --> 00:08:26.643
Durant's, look at that!

00:08:26.643 --> 00:08:28.723
You got to be kiddin' me.

00:08:28.723 --> 00:08:30.360
- I just try to make it about the team,

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:31.962
make it about my teammates, it's not fair

00:08:31.962 --> 00:08:36.129
to the organization and to my
teammates to be distracted.

00:08:37.038 --> 00:08:39.281
I have to be the best me I can be,

00:08:39.281 --> 00:08:42.687
and, I think, I was proud of how

00:08:42.687 --> 00:08:44.633
I was able to stay in the moment,

00:08:44.633 --> 00:08:47.050
that's been a struggle for me

00:08:47.911 --> 00:08:50.670
as a young player in this league.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:53.503
So I was stayin' conscious
of bein' in the moment

00:08:53.503 --> 00:08:55.802
and I was proud of how I stayed there,

00:08:55.802 --> 00:09:00.571
especially throughout the
playoffs and the regular season.

00:09:00.571 --> 00:09:03.806
It was just all about worryin' about today

00:09:03.806 --> 00:09:06.417
and once tomorrow get there,
I'll worry about that.

00:09:06.417 --> 00:09:08.815
That's who I've been the last few years,

00:09:08.815 --> 00:09:10.982
just takin' it day by day.

00:09:11.903 --> 00:09:14.253
- [Announcer] Achieving cult
status right now in Dallas

00:09:14.253 --> 00:09:15.717
after his last two performances.

00:09:15.717 --> 00:09:16.550
Durant!

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:17.800
Oh, and a foul!

00:09:18.710 --> 00:09:20.679
- [Announcer] Kevin Durant throws it down.

00:09:20.679 --> 00:09:21.512
- [Announcer] My goodness,

00:09:21.512 --> 00:09:23.432
Kevin Durant says to Brendan Haywood,

00:09:23.432 --> 00:09:26.580
"Excuse me, I got an
appointment with the rim."

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:30.015
- The odds were stacked against us,

00:09:30.015 --> 00:09:32.215
single parent with two boys,

00:09:32.215 --> 00:09:34.965
by the time we were 21 years old,

00:09:37.166 --> 00:09:39.088
everybody told us, "We
weren't supposed to be here."

00:09:39.088 --> 00:09:42.171
We moved from apartment to apartment,

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:44.143
by ourselves.

00:09:45.022 --> 00:09:46.938
One of the best memories
I had, is when we moved

00:09:46.938 --> 00:09:49.021
into our first apartment,

00:09:51.984 --> 00:09:53.651
no bed, no furniture

00:09:54.584 --> 00:09:57.239
and we just all sat in the living room

00:09:57.239 --> 00:10:00.290
and just hugged each other,

00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:03.040
because, we thought we'd made it.

00:10:06.022 --> 00:10:09.167
And when something good happens to you,

00:10:09.167 --> 00:10:11.678
I don't know about you guys,
but I tend to look back

00:10:11.678 --> 00:10:13.678
to what brought me here.

00:10:16.698 --> 00:10:18.977
And you wake me up in
the middle of the night,

00:10:18.977 --> 00:10:22.505
in the summertimes,
makin' me run up the hill,

00:10:22.505 --> 00:10:26.201
makin' me do push-ups, screamin'
at me from the sidelines

00:10:26.201 --> 00:10:29.451
of my games at eight or nine years old.

00:10:30.332 --> 00:10:32.800
We wasn't supposed to be here.

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:36.785
You made us believe, you
kept us off the street,

00:10:36.785 --> 00:10:40.596
put clothes on our
backs, food on the table.

00:10:40.596 --> 00:10:43.812
When you didn't eat, you made sure we ate.

00:10:43.812 --> 00:10:46.219
You went to sleep hungry.

00:10:46.219 --> 00:10:50.151
You sacrificed for us. (crying)

00:10:50.151 --> 00:10:52.561
You're the real MVP.

00:10:52.561 --> 00:10:54.811
(applause)

00:11:00.845 --> 00:11:03.016
- [Announcer] Here is Durant for the win!

00:11:03.016 --> 00:11:04.052
(cheering)

00:11:04.052 --> 00:11:05.052
Kevin Durant

00:11:06.235 --> 00:11:07.288
has won

00:11:07.288 --> 00:11:08.455
at the buzzer!

00:11:09.813 --> 00:11:12.821
- [Announcer] What a sensational play

00:11:12.821 --> 00:11:15.555
and shot by Kevin Durant!

00:11:15.555 --> 00:11:18.805
That's how you win games at the buzzer!

00:11:23.857 --> 00:11:25.483
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:11:25.483 --> 00:11:28.011
- We made this video because
Robin Sharma asked us to.

00:11:28.011 --> 00:11:29.773
If you'd like us to profile someone else,

00:11:29.773 --> 00:11:31.093
leave a message in the comments below.

00:11:31.093 --> 00:11:32.641
- I'd also love to know which

00:11:32.641 --> 00:11:34.664
of the top 10 rules meant the most to you,

00:11:34.664 --> 00:11:36.978
had the biggest impact,
leave in the comments

00:11:36.978 --> 00:11:38.313
and we'll join in the discussion.

00:11:38.313 --> 00:11:40.011
So thank you guys again for watching,

00:11:40.011 --> 00:11:42.020
continue to believe,

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:43.937
and we'll see you soon.

00:11:49.217 --> 00:11:53.004
- My game is based upon bein' versatile,

00:11:53.004 --> 00:11:55.646
I think, you know, my biggest attribute,

00:11:55.646 --> 00:11:57.887
is scorin' the basketball.

00:11:57.887 --> 00:12:00.606
I think I find the rim in different ways.

00:12:00.606 --> 00:12:02.689
I think I'm a shot maker.

00:12:03.576 --> 00:12:05.638
I can play inside and out, I'm
still workin' on both parts

00:12:05.638 --> 00:12:07.840
of my game, I'm far
from where I want to be.

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:12.108
But, with my length and my
size, I can play inside and out.

00:12:12.108 --> 00:12:13.979
I think about the future a lot,

00:12:13.979 --> 00:12:17.388
the steps I have to take
now for us to, maybe,

00:12:17.388 --> 00:12:19.299
be a championship team.

00:12:19.299 --> 00:12:20.458
Or, what it's goin' to look like for me

00:12:20.458 --> 00:12:23.369
in three or four years, what I'm be doin',

00:12:23.369 --> 00:12:24.753
or where I'm be at.

00:12:24.753 --> 00:12:26.353
What team I'm play for.

00:12:26.353 --> 00:12:29.886
I never thought I'd be
able to impact people,

00:12:29.886 --> 00:12:31.473
the way I have so far.

00:12:31.473 --> 00:12:33.442
I take pride in that.

00:12:33.442 --> 00:12:35.386
I'm just a regular guy,

00:12:35.386 --> 00:12:37.500
I play ball on TV sometimes.

00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:39.854
And knowin' I can give
'em hope and inspire 'em,

00:12:39.854 --> 00:12:42.381
has been somethin' that's
been like a dream come true.

00:12:42.381 --> 00:12:44.198
- [Player] One, two, three!

00:12:44.198 --> 00:12:45.906
- [Crowd] Strong and kind!

